WEBVTT

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:05.750
Spring Summer Autumn Winter, fly by quickly.
haru natsu aki fuyu ashibaya ni kakenu keteku

00:00:05.780 --> 00:00:13.730
Today and tomorrow. Everyday is an endless festival.
kyou mo ashita mo mainichi zutto FESTIVAL

00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:28.070
When pink flower petals dance around
pinku no hanabira harari mau goro

00:00:28.110 --> 00:00:33.980
there will be many encounters and farewells
deai mo wakare mo iro iro aruyo ne

00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:39.220
The brilliant sun scorches the ground
sansan ohisama jimen jirijiri

00:00:39.290 --> 00:00:44.290
To the sea! To the mountains! A hot premonition.
umi ikou yama ikou atsui yokan

00:00:44.290 --> 00:00:50.500
Wherever we go, the essentials follow.
doko he yuku ni mo zettai ni hitsuyou na

00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:53.270
The smiles, the friends are there.
egao ga iru nakama ga iru

00:00:53.270 --> 00:00:56.170
How wonderful!
nante suteki nano

00:00:57.440 --> 00:01:02.940
Enter laughter, enter three sisters,
warai no sanjou sannin shimai sanjou

00:01:03.010 --> 00:01:08.550
A big explosion! A Daimyo's procession is passing by,
daibakuhatsu daimyou gyouretsu toorimasu

00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:14.120
Spring Summer Autumn Winter; each splendid in their own ways
haru natsu aki fuyu jitsu ni sorazore subarashii

00:01:14.150 --> 00:01:21.330
Today and tomorrow. Everyday an endless festival.
kyou mo ashita mo mainichi zutto FESTIVAL

00:01:22.160 --> 00:01:27.600
A festival all year around.
nen gara nen juu FESTIVAL

00:01:30.370 --> 00:01:35.370
I'll take it

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:47.750
I guess people would want to eat something hot.

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:50.320
Should I bring a stove to school?

00:01:51.890 --> 00:01:53.930
No, no, that wouldn't be very smart.

00:01:54.860 --> 00:01:57.430
What if I put some quicklime underneath it?

00:01:57.900 --> 00:01:59.670
It should heat up very quickly.

00:02:06.370 --> 00:02:08.010
Okay, that should do.

00:02:08.670 --> 00:02:10.580
Super deluxe surprise hotpot lunchbox.

00:02:10.580 --> 00:02:14.080
Looks like this won't go very well.

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:16.650
Hosaka~!

00:02:17.250 --> 00:02:18.320
Oh, Hayami.

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:24.020
You're putting a lot of thought into this, but do you really think Haruka-chan would be happy with this?

00:02:24.020 --> 00:02:24.790
What?

00:02:25.420 --> 00:02:31.060
Right now, you and Haruka-chan are cooking for completely different reasons.

00:02:31.060 --> 00:02:33.830
Just asking, but what do you mean?

00:02:35.170 --> 00:02:39.070
Haruka-chan cooks with love. You cook with ego.

00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:43.710
Currently, you couldn't even satisfy an insect.

00:02:51.680 --> 00:02:56.290
I was wondering what you were trying to say, but my love is true.

00:02:58.690 --> 00:03:01.490
Hosaka, your feelings are purer and stronger than anyone else's.

00:03:01.490 --> 00:03:02.800
Ego, she says.
Hosaka, your feelings are purer and stronger than anyone else's.

00:03:02.800 --> 00:03:03.300
Hosaka, your feelings are purer and stronger than anyone else's.

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:04.400
That was amusing.
That was amusing.

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:06.400
I know that better than anyone.

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:06.970
Total nonsense.
I know that better than anyone.

00:03:06.970 --> 00:03:07.770
Total nonsense.

00:03:08.430 --> 00:03:13.740
But realize this, Hosaka, your way of expressing your feelings is a bit... misguided.

00:03:14.470 --> 00:03:18.180
No, gravely misguided.

00:03:31.890 --> 00:03:32.890
Hosaka-senpa-

00:03:49.510 --> 00:03:54.450
Haruka-neesama said she would make meat stew today.

00:03:54.450 --> 00:03:55.050
Hmm?

00:03:55.050 --> 00:03:57.650
Paper:  Beef - Carrots

00:03:59.250 --> 00:04:01.750
Sign:  Carrots

00:04:02.220 --> 00:04:06.430
I guess it's something that can't be made without carrots...

00:04:06.830 --> 00:04:09.660
Carrots add vivid coloring to a dish normally lacking it.

00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:12.930
However, they're not all for show.

00:04:13.400 --> 00:04:15.830
They're full of necessary nutrients too.

00:04:16.770 --> 00:04:20.140
I haven't noticed until just now, but carrots are splendid.

00:04:21.210 --> 00:04:22.140
I see...

00:04:23.410 --> 00:04:25.210
This is full of love!

00:04:26.310 --> 00:04:27.210
I'll take it.

00:04:36.360 --> 00:04:38.020
Love... huh...

00:04:39.690 --> 00:04:40.790
I'll take it.

00:04:53.570 --> 00:04:56.310
Even today, Keiko was so...

00:04:57.980 --> 00:05:00.810
Oh! This stew is delicious!

00:05:01.480 --> 00:05:02.820
Thank you.

00:05:13.260 --> 00:05:14.460
So, you see...

00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:15.030
Oh?

00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:30.940
Chiaki!

00:05:34.250 --> 00:05:35.750
Not bad, Chiaki!

00:05:35.750 --> 00:05:37.420
You tried hard, didn't you, Chiaki?

00:05:39.990 --> 00:05:42.090
Because it's love.

00:05:54.400 --> 00:05:57.700
Hosaka. You're holding something, aren't you?

00:05:57.700 --> 00:05:58.440
Yeah.

00:06:00.970 --> 00:06:03.810
My carrot-filled meat stew lunch box.

00:06:03.810 --> 00:06:05.080
Try it for me.

00:06:05.440 --> 00:06:08.050
Eh? Why me?

00:06:09.010 --> 00:06:10.850
There is no need for words anymore.

00:06:11.420 --> 00:06:16.490
If you taste this, you will have no doubts about my love for Minami Haruka.

00:06:16.490 --> 00:06:19.020
Say "Ah."

00:06:19.020 --> 00:06:21.690
I get it! I get it already!

00:06:21.690 --> 00:06:25.100
No, if you eat this, you will understand even more!

00:06:25.100 --> 00:06:27.830
Here, say "Ah!"

00:06:31.040 --> 00:06:34.540
NO!

00:06:40.380 --> 00:06:43.180
Is something wrong, Haruka? You seem very happy.

00:06:44.580 --> 00:06:49.090
Yesterday, Chiaki ate all the carrots in the meat stew.

00:06:49.490 --> 00:06:53.660
So thinking of what to cook next is a lot of fun.

00:06:57.430 --> 00:06:58.600
I know!

00:07:00.070 --> 00:07:02.570
Let's have carrot steak tonight!

00:07:03.440 --> 00:07:06.310
Maybe some carrot sticks...

00:07:06.310 --> 00:07:09.540
Oh, and some carrot juice too!

00:07:09.540 --> 00:07:11.380
Ah... That's...

00:07:11.880 --> 00:07:14.810
Haruka, you might want to take it slowly.

00:07:20.790 --> 00:07:25.790
Could be

00:07:28.530 --> 00:07:30.260
Hello!

00:07:30.500 --> 00:07:32.130
Hey, Yoshino!

00:07:32.130 --> 00:07:33.130
Welcome.

00:07:33.130 --> 00:07:36.540
Chiaki's gone shopping, so you'll have to wait a while.

00:07:36.840 --> 00:07:37.870
Okay.

00:07:40.810 --> 00:07:42.310
What was that again...

00:07:42.310 --> 00:07:43.940
Hm? What's wrong?

00:07:43.940 --> 00:07:48.680
I remembered it just now, but then I forgot again.

00:07:48.680 --> 00:07:50.950
Hmm, that's a bit concerning.

00:07:51.780 --> 00:07:52.880
Hey, Kana.

00:07:54.290 --> 00:07:57.460
Do you think Yoshino has realized who I really am?

00:07:58.320 --> 00:08:00.860
And now I can't remember it at all.

00:08:00.860 --> 00:08:02.960
Ah, yeah, that happens.

00:08:02.960 --> 00:08:05.230
Really... Forgetting things is pretty strange, isn't it?

00:08:05.230 --> 00:08:06.300
Unlike Uchida, Yoshino is smart, so she probably already knows.
Really... Forgetting things is pretty strange, isn't it?

00:08:06.300 --> 00:08:09.170
Unlike Uchida, Yoshino is smart, so she probably already knows.

00:08:09.600 --> 00:08:13.910
But I don't think she'd spill it even if she knew.

00:08:13.910 --> 00:08:15.840
Eh? Why's that?

00:08:16.240 --> 00:08:20.350
Because of the Yoshino theory that is the most prominent now!

00:08:20.610 --> 00:08:23.120
S-such a theory even exists?

00:08:23.120 --> 00:08:24.920
Only inside my head.

00:08:25.350 --> 00:08:29.050
Yoshino thinks it's funny, seeing you in girl's clothes.

00:08:29.050 --> 00:08:30.160
W-Why?

00:08:30.790 --> 00:08:33.890
If she revealed it, it wouldn't be funny anymore!

00:08:35.360 --> 00:08:41.070
Well, this is only if she really knows that you are Makoto.

00:08:41.630 --> 00:08:45.240
I-If you say that...

00:08:49.070 --> 00:08:51.580
I can't see her as a human!

00:09:03.120 --> 00:09:08.130
At school, they told us not to forget to bring something tomorrow.

00:09:08.130 --> 00:09:09.830
What was it again...?

00:09:10.230 --> 00:09:10.830
Hey.

00:09:12.130 --> 00:09:14.770
I'm a middle schooler, so I wouldn't know.

00:09:17.270 --> 00:09:22.510
Sorry. I had a weird feeling that you were in the same year as me.

00:09:25.780 --> 00:09:29.950
She's begun to take action because she knows the truth.

00:09:30.350 --> 00:09:31.920
Or so it seems.

00:09:32.720 --> 00:09:35.920
So she's basically found out then, Kana?

00:09:35.920 --> 00:09:38.620
Not so fast. It's still too soon to draw conclusions.

00:09:39.490 --> 00:09:43.460
She could've really thought that you were in the same grade as she was.

00:09:43.900 --> 00:09:45.200
That's right.

00:09:45.200 --> 00:09:48.870
It's possible I naturally seem like that.

00:09:48.870 --> 00:09:52.370
By the way, Kana, have you cleaned the bathtub yet?

00:09:53.110 --> 00:09:55.870
Not yet.  We have guests right now, so I'll do it later.

00:09:55.870 --> 00:09:58.880
No. Do it before you have fun.

00:09:59.280 --> 00:10:00.910
But...

00:10:00.910 --> 00:10:04.620
Mako-chan will be with us, so don't worry about her.

00:10:04.920 --> 00:10:06.650
I-I guess...

00:10:08.450 --> 00:10:11.660
Then, Mako-chan, I'll be cleaning the bath.

00:10:12.460 --> 00:10:13.190
Good luck.

00:10:14.260 --> 00:10:15.760
I'll do it!

00:10:16.560 --> 00:10:20.000
You're always looking after me, so something like this is no big deal.

00:10:20.530 --> 00:10:21.600
Mako-chan...

00:10:29.710 --> 00:10:32.180
I'll work alone for now.

00:10:34.180 --> 00:10:36.410
I'll help you out, Mako-chan.

00:10:36.750 --> 00:10:39.520
Since they're always looking after me too.

00:10:39.520 --> 00:10:40.220
Ah...

00:10:40.220 --> 00:10:41.120
Yes?

00:10:41.120 --> 00:10:43.460
Your skirt's almost touching the floor.

00:10:45.020 --> 00:10:46.560
I'll handle the scrubbing then.

00:10:47.990 --> 00:10:49.760
The skirt's fine!

00:10:49.760 --> 00:10:52.430
Yoshino, you can go warm up under the kotatsu.

00:10:52.430 --> 00:10:53.830
Eh? But...

00:10:53.830 --> 00:10:55.130
It's fine.

00:10:55.130 --> 00:10:56.500
It's okay, I'll help.

00:10:56.500 --> 00:10:58.670
I said I'll do it.

00:10:58.940 --> 00:11:04.180
I'll do it.

00:11:12.480 --> 00:11:14.550
I heard a loud noise just now, but...

00:11:21.860 --> 00:11:24.000
What happened? Are you okay?

00:11:24.700 --> 00:11:26.360
I'm okay...

00:11:29.070 --> 00:11:30.070
Mako-chan.

00:11:30.700 --> 00:11:32.340
You're strong.

00:11:32.340 --> 00:11:33.910
That surprised me.

00:11:33.910 --> 00:11:36.510
It's almost like you're a boy.

00:11:44.520 --> 00:11:46.820
What exactly happened in the bathtub?

00:11:47.350 --> 00:11:48.750
Enough.

00:11:50.090 --> 00:11:52.190
I've had enough!

00:11:55.060 --> 00:11:57.800
Yoshino, you already know, right?

00:11:57.800 --> 00:11:59.030
Let's hear it.

00:12:10.510 --> 00:12:11.180
Yeah.

00:12:11.740 --> 00:12:12.840
I know.

00:12:18.720 --> 00:12:21.890
I have to remember to bring my protractor to school tomorrow!

00:12:23.260 --> 00:12:26.460
Well, I'm a middle schooler, so...

00:12:32.860 --> 00:12:37.870
Motivation

00:12:50.850 --> 00:12:53.990
It's almost that time again!

00:12:57.990 --> 00:12:59.360
And so...

00:12:59.360 --> 00:13:04.660
Today, I've invited an expert with seventeen years of Valentine's Day experience.

00:13:06.100 --> 00:13:07.330
It's Maki-sensei.

00:13:07.930 --> 00:13:09.070
Hello, good day.

00:13:09.930 --> 00:13:11.770
Do you want to win on Valentine's Day!?

00:13:12.070 --> 00:13:13.470
I want to win!

00:13:13.810 --> 00:13:15.310
Do you want to win no matter what?

00:13:15.310 --> 00:13:16.610
I want to win!

00:13:16.610 --> 00:13:18.240
How do you win?

00:13:22.710 --> 00:13:27.320
Uchida-kun, what do you think boys want the most on Valentine's Day?

00:13:31.560 --> 00:13:35.090
To receive chocolate from the person he likes?

00:13:35.360 --> 00:13:38.800
The correct answer is chocolate from anyone at all.

00:13:40.270 --> 00:13:43.970
No matter who it's from, they'll be happy if they get chocolate.

00:13:43.970 --> 00:13:49.440
Sensei, so you're saying there's a chance even if you give chocolate to someone you don't know, right?

00:13:49.440 --> 00:13:49.940
Yep.

00:13:50.440 --> 00:13:51.280
Question.

00:13:52.310 --> 00:13:53.780
Go ahead, Chiaki-kun.

00:13:54.110 --> 00:13:59.020
Wouldn't you be afraid if you suddenly got chocolate from a stranger?

00:14:01.720 --> 00:14:05.790
Maki-sensei, Chiaki isn't exactly suited to all this Valentine's Day stuff.

00:14:05.790 --> 00:14:07.030
So let's leave her out.

00:14:18.570 --> 00:14:22.810
For me, I've been eating stranger's chocolate since I was little,

00:14:22.810 --> 00:14:24.780
so I have nothing against it.

00:14:24.780 --> 00:14:26.480
What do you mean?

00:14:26.480 --> 00:14:30.220
My brothers always give me the chocolate they receive.

00:14:32.220 --> 00:14:39.460
I always thought that guys were supposed to give chocolates on Valentine's Day.

00:14:39.720 --> 00:14:43.330
Maki-sensei, Touma has been cultured differently than us.

00:14:43.330 --> 00:14:44.500
So let's leave her out.

00:14:55.910 --> 00:14:59.410
Hey, hey. Sensei, can I ask a question.

00:14:59.410 --> 00:15:00.680
Yes, Uchida-kun.

00:15:01.050 --> 00:15:06.280
I don't know any boys whom I want to give chocolates to this year.

00:15:06.280 --> 00:15:07.890
What should I do?

00:15:14.590 --> 00:15:17.430
What are you doing, Kana?

00:15:17.900 --> 00:15:24.670
I hereby curse you so that when you give chocolate to your prince, his white horse will eat it!

00:15:27.140 --> 00:15:29.110
Just joking.

00:15:37.180 --> 00:15:42.450
Damn! My students aren't motivated anymore because of me.

00:15:43.150 --> 00:15:44.390
This is bad...

00:15:44.760 --> 00:15:48.630
My plan to make chocolate with everyone

00:15:48.630 --> 00:15:51.000
and then secretly eat it is going to fail.

00:15:51.500 --> 00:15:53.830
I have to change the mood somehow...

00:15:53.830 --> 00:15:57.400
Maki-sensei! Tell us your loveliest Valentine's story!

00:15:57.400 --> 00:15:57.840
Eh?

00:16:13.950 --> 00:16:15.050
She doesn't have one!

00:16:16.550 --> 00:16:18.960
And no one is left.

00:16:22.230 --> 00:16:23.760
I'm back.

00:16:24.260 --> 00:16:27.200
I got some chocolate from a store.

00:16:27.200 --> 00:16:29.170
Let's all try it out.

00:16:35.010 --> 00:16:36.540
This is pretty good.

00:16:37.380 --> 00:16:39.780
I think I'll visit this store.

00:16:39.780 --> 00:16:42.750
Well, I ended up getting chocolate, so it's fine.

00:16:44.880 --> 00:16:46.750
Ah. He came.

00:16:46.750 --> 00:16:47.150
He came while we were eating chocolate.

00:16:47.150 --> 00:16:48.590
Yes, Haruka-neesama.
He came while we were eating chocolate.

00:16:48.590 --> 00:16:49.020
What good timing.
Yes, Haruka-neesama.

00:16:49.020 --> 00:16:50.190
What good timing.

00:16:50.190 --> 00:16:51.620
Thank you very much.
Thank you very much.

00:16:52.220 --> 00:16:52.960
Who is it?

00:16:53.690 --> 00:16:55.130
Probably Fujioka.

00:16:58.730 --> 00:17:01.570
Oh no! Everyone, hurry up and finish the chocolate!

00:17:04.840 --> 00:17:07.170
Chiaki-chan, hurry up and hide the box.

00:17:07.570 --> 00:17:08.640
O-Okay.

00:17:11.580 --> 00:17:14.080
I wonder if I should drink something.

00:17:14.080 --> 00:17:15.050
Why?

00:17:17.280 --> 00:17:19.020
What's going on?

00:17:19.020 --> 00:17:19.880
Kana-chan!

00:17:20.720 --> 00:17:24.390
It's courtesy to not let boys see any Valentine preparation!

00:17:28.160 --> 00:17:29.630
I'm sorry.

00:17:31.200 --> 00:17:33.830
For some reason, it seems everyone's really motivated.

00:17:48.150 --> 00:17:53.150
Possible Things

00:18:01.760 --> 00:18:02.560
I see.

00:18:03.090 --> 00:18:04.760
It's almost Valentine's Day.

00:18:06.500 --> 00:18:12.070
If she finds my arms full of chocolate on Valentine's Day,

00:18:12.770 --> 00:18:15.310
she might hesitate to give me some.

00:18:16.370 --> 00:18:21.050
In that case, I must keep my right arm open for her at all times!

00:18:22.550 --> 00:18:27.220
But all the boys at school wear the same uniform.

00:18:28.150 --> 00:18:31.190
Will she be able to find me out of all of them?

00:18:31.890 --> 00:18:37.760
In that case, I'll keep my right arm open, holding a rose in my left to show where I am.

00:18:39.500 --> 00:18:44.340
But will she notice the rose?

00:18:45.700 --> 00:18:46.200
I see. It's almost Valentine's day.

00:18:46.200 --> 00:18:49.010
In that case, I will...!
I see. It's almost Valentine's day.

00:18:49.010 --> 00:18:49.510
In that case, I will...!

00:18:52.380 --> 00:18:56.250
So, from whom do you want Valentine's Day chocolate the most?

00:18:58.820 --> 00:19:04.690
Maki-sensei, I thought it was supposed to be courtesy to not discuss Valentine's day in front of a boy.

00:19:04.690 --> 00:19:06.720
Don't be so uptight.

00:19:06.720 --> 00:19:10.560
We should listen to what guys think about Valentine's Day too.

00:19:10.560 --> 00:19:11.800
That's true.

00:19:12.160 --> 00:19:15.070
Although they don't appear to show anything physically,

00:19:15.070 --> 00:19:20.040
Valentine's Day seems to be of great concern on the inside.

00:19:20.710 --> 00:19:23.740
At the mention of the words "Valentine's Day" just now,

00:19:23.740 --> 00:19:26.210
Fujioka's muscles stiffened.

00:19:27.180 --> 00:19:29.380
His body reacted, huh.

00:19:32.880 --> 00:19:34.020
Kana-chan!

00:19:35.850 --> 00:19:38.160
I bet she's stealing food from the kitchen.

00:19:38.160 --> 00:19:39.990
He stiffened up again.

00:19:45.360 --> 00:19:46.460
Fujioka-kun.

00:19:46.460 --> 00:19:47.900
Y-Yes?

00:19:47.900 --> 00:19:52.700
You might be thinking that just because you're a guy, you can't choose whom to give chocolates to.

00:19:53.870 --> 00:19:55.410
But that's not true.

00:19:56.040 --> 00:19:59.010
Do your best! You should be able to do something about that!

00:19:59.340 --> 00:20:00.580
Do your best!

00:20:02.210 --> 00:20:03.450
What I can do...

00:20:08.550 --> 00:20:11.560
The Next day

00:20:11.890 --> 00:20:12.760
Minami!

00:20:14.690 --> 00:20:15.990
Fujioka.

00:20:15.990 --> 00:20:19.160
That looks heavy. Shall I take it for you?

00:20:19.160 --> 00:20:21.100
Eh? But...

00:20:21.100 --> 00:20:22.030
It's fine.

00:20:24.700 --> 00:20:26.540
Then... here.

00:20:42.490 --> 00:20:45.120
And the next day

00:20:45.490 --> 00:20:46.320
Minami!

00:20:47.560 --> 00:20:49.260
It must be hard doing it alone.

00:20:49.630 --> 00:20:50.730
Let me help you!

00:20:53.400 --> 00:20:54.000
Here.

00:21:07.450 --> 00:21:09.350
And the day after that

00:21:09.780 --> 00:21:10.720
Minami!

00:21:12.250 --> 00:21:13.820
What are you in a hurry for?

00:21:13.820 --> 00:21:15.390
I'll run for you!

00:21:16.790 --> 00:21:17.660
But...

00:21:24.900 --> 00:21:25.630
Uh...

00:21:31.740 --> 00:21:35.140
Fujioka's has been acting really weird recently...

00:21:36.240 --> 00:21:38.410
What happened to him?

00:21:40.040 --> 00:21:45.580
Riko said he's got a soccer match soon, so he might be tired because of practice.

00:21:45.580 --> 00:21:47.750
I see. So that's it.

00:21:50.590 --> 00:21:52.660
Valentine's Day is tomorrow, huh.

00:21:55.490 --> 00:21:58.460
I've got to try my best tomorrow... Tomorrow...

00:22:02.330 --> 00:22:05.100
On Valentine's Day

00:22:08.410 --> 00:22:09.710
Good morning, Fujioka!

00:22:11.740 --> 00:22:13.210
Good morning, Minami.

00:22:13.210 --> 00:22:16.780
Fujioka, I've got something to give you today.

00:22:19.480 --> 00:22:19.950
Here.

00:22:21.490 --> 00:22:24.260
When you're tired, you should eat something sweet.

00:22:25.290 --> 00:22:25.920
Here!

00:22:27.530 --> 00:22:28.530
Thank you.

00:22:38.400 --> 00:22:40.570
You gave chocolate to Fujioka-kun.

00:22:41.140 --> 00:22:43.410
And I thought you weren't interested in Valentine's Day.

00:22:45.140 --> 00:22:46.640
That was today?

00:22:50.850 --> 00:22:54.020
You forgot?! Then what was that chocolate for?!

00:22:54.850 --> 00:22:56.650
Chocolate for when you're tired!

00:23:27.020 --> 00:23:28.050
Thank you!
arigatou

00:23:28.050 --> 00:23:30.920
Now that I made it this far,
koko made koreta yorokobi wo

00:23:30.920 --> 00:23:33.860
I wanted to tell you that straight away
massugu ni kimi ni todoketai

00:23:34.160 --> 00:23:38.530
Put your thoughts into the southern wind
minami kaze ni omoi komete iku yo

00:23:38.730 --> 00:23:40.500
Let's go! And smile!
egao ni nare

00:23:45.700 --> 00:23:48.610
"Ordinary days are also special"
nante koto nai hibi ga

00:23:48.610 --> 00:23:51.480
tokubetsu datte koto wo
"Ordinary days are also special"

00:23:51.880 --> 00:23:55.050
The one that taught me that was you
oshiete kureta no wa kimi

00:23:55.750 --> 00:23:57.520
Thank you! Thank you!
arigatou sankyuu

00:23:57.520 --> 00:24:02.990
Briskly and confidently put on your apron
tekipaki epuron souchaku jishin motte

00:24:03.590 --> 00:24:08.560
Let's passionately do the things we like.
omoi kiri suki na koto wo yarimashou

00:24:09.060 --> 00:24:15.070
I'm home!　I always wanted to meet you.
tadaima itsudatte aitaku naru yo

00:24:15.070 --> 00:24:19.400
Because you, the important one, are here.
taisetsu na kimi ga iru kara

00:24:19.700 --> 00:24:23.540
Tears are sparkling, as the future is shining
namida mo kirakira mirai de kagayaku.

00:24:23.540 --> 00:24:26.480
Because goodbyes are beginnings
sayonara wa hajimari dakara

00:24:26.480 --> 00:24:31.620
Let's dream, with a little anticipation
chotto dake kitai shite yume mimashou

00:24:31.620 --> 00:24:35.350
Always hold those you love in your heart
itsumo daisuki wo mune ni aruiteku

00:24:35.350 --> 00:24:38.290
Don't let go of your hot feelings
attakai kimochi wo hanasanai

00:24:38.560 --> 00:24:41.430
Put your thoughts into the southern wind
minami kaze ni omoi komete

00:24:41.430 --> 00:24:43.430
Let's go together!
issho ni ikou yo

00:24:44.030 --> 00:24:47.870
Thank you! And smile!
arigatou egao ni nare
